==Battleground==
*1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Crazed Titan Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Titan Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**8 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[Li'l Nyandam (Enemy)|Li'l Nyandam]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Success on this boss party of a stage depends entirely on outlasting the enemies. [[Octopus Cat]] is nearly mandatory to negate the [[Wave Attack]]s made by Crazed Titan, and can also serve as a tank against the Li'l Bun Buns. The main threat on this stage is fighting Crazed Titan and Li'l Nyandam at the same time. Strong meatshield lines combined with tanky units, as well as a few long-range assault units, can spell doom for the bosses. It may help to focus on one enemy at a time – taking out Li'l Nyandam first will make dealing with Crazed Titan much easier, for example.

Decently-levelled Octopus Cats can stall Dark Emperor Nyandam and Teacher Bun Bun indefinitely, allowing for money to be maxed out before taking on the rest of the enemies. Be sure not to spawn too many Octopus Cats, as they might kill Bun Bun too quickly. Pair the Octopuses with meatshields and some [[:Category:Super-Backliner-class Cats|super-backliners]] units like [[Cyberpunk Cat]] for victory!

